-- 0005_kyiv_clock: winter sunrise and sunset times that were taken on UTC+3, which is Moscow time from the
-- last Sunday of October to the last Sunday of March, while Ukraine keeps EET (UTC+2). Found when the Vuhledar
-- diorama moved to Kyiv time (design/next-items.md §5 decision 6): every sunrise and sunset claim was recomputed
-- with the NOAA solar equations. Ukrainian-held places in winter (Vuhledar, Bakhmut, Avdiivka, Pokrovsk,
-- Mariupol in early March 2022, Krynky's foothold) and two A-50 claims were an hour late; the Kyiv-region,
-- Brovary, Stepove, Orikhiv, Kharkiv and summer claims were right, and occupied Crimea's own clock is left as
-- stated. Each correction is the recorded time less one hour. Idempotent: every update matches the old text.

UPDATE claim:cc08_0018_08 SET text = string::replace(text, "sunrise was about 07:50 and sunset about 17:40 local time.", "sunrise was about 06:50 and sunset about 16:40 Kyiv time (EET, UTC+2)."), confidence_note = "Clock corrected (2026-10-14): the reanalysis times were taken on UTC+3, which is Moscow time in winter; Ukraine keeps EET (UTC+2) from the last Sunday of October to the last Sunday of March. Recomputed with the NOAA solar equations; the corrected times are the recorded ones less one hour." WHERE text CONTAINS "sunrise was about 07:50 and sunset about 17:40 local time.";
UPDATE claim:cc08_0018_03 SET text = string::replace(text, "sunset fell from about 17:19 to 16:48 local time between 28 October and 20 November 2022.", "sunset fell from about 17:19 (summer time, UTC+3) to 15:48 Kyiv time (UTC+2) between 28 October and 20 November 2022; the clocks went back on 30 October."), confidence_note = "Clock corrected (2026-10-14): the reanalysis times were taken on UTC+3, which is Moscow time in winter; Ukraine keeps EET (UTC+2) from the last Sunday of October to the last Sunday of March. Recomputed with the NOAA solar equations; the corrected times are the recorded ones less one hour." WHERE text CONTAINS "sunset fell from about 17:19 to 16:48 local time between 28 October and 20 November 2022.";
UPDATE claim:cc07_0019_04 SET text = string::replace(text, "mid-month sunrise 07:35 and sunset 16:48.", "mid-month sunrise 06:35 and sunset 15:48 (Kyiv time)."), confidence_note = "Clock corrected (2026-10-14): the reanalysis times were taken on UTC+3, which is Moscow time in winter; Ukraine keeps EET (UTC+2) from the last Sunday of October to the last Sunday of March. Recomputed with the NOAA solar equations; the corrected times are the recorded ones less one hour." WHERE text CONTAINS "mid-month sunrise 07:35 and sunset 16:48.";
